## 10a. Amendments during implementation (logged in the notebook)

(A1, 2026-09-15 15:5x, from the Codex round-5/integrative review, blockers 9–10) **exp_07 edits no pre-existing module.** The branch's edits to `train_xRIR_backbone.py`, `tools/provenance.py`, `tools/exp04_eval.py`, `tools/exp04_eval_launch.py`, `tools/exp04_launcher.py`, `tools/exp05_probe.py`, `tools/exp05_gates.py`, `tools/results_table.py` and `tools/yaw_aug.py` are reverted to main's bytes, because (i) exp_04's bound record re-hashes its evaluator/writer closure files against the live tree, so any change to those files breaks `check_record.py`, and (ii) exp_06's filled approvals and its parser-contract test pin the shared trainer and evaluation modules. The same reviewed behaviour is relocated to exp_07-specific modules that IMPORT the shared ones unchanged: `tools/exp07_train.py` (entry point: imports the trainer module and both dataset classes, selects the class by `--protocol`, records `protocol` in `args.json`/runtime args, delegates to the trainer's `main()`; the training closure is derived from this entry point and thus contains the seen module), `tools/exp07_provenance.py` (protocol-aware inventory, `seen_split_identity`), `tools/exp07_launcher.py` + `tools/exp07_launch.sh` (the seen arms, goldens calling `tools/exp07_train.py`, per-arm comparators, one-retry, receipts), `tools/exp07_probe.py` / `tools/exp07_gates.py`, `tools/exp07_eval.py` (its own run loop composed from `eval_yaw_rotation`'s and `tools.exp04_eval`'s functions, seen dataset factory, split handshake), `tools/exp07_eval_launch.py` (seen routing and `seen_split` binding), `tools/exp07_audit.py` (the seen alignment audit), and exp_07's own Markdown writer. §3's file table is read with this relocation; the reviewed logic and tests carry over.

